[{"id":"VRCE-6-73-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":1,"english":"When things were in this condition, Rāvana's younger brother addressed Lakşmaņa in words fraught with evil to foes and conducing to the welfare (of his own party), saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9b18aafbc3d4035c791e8e894471c98a9b23e50e799b73c9834c881ca3e921d8","compact":"13ee88d37fd4505156d9cf179b38f045dc1fdd687546930aa8c253f6664f6ddf","nasal":"13ee88d37fd4505156d9cf179b38f045dc1fdd687546930aa8c253f6664f6ddf"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":2,"english":"Do you without delay bring on an engagement between this cloud-black Räksasa army, which you behold, and the monkeys having rocks for their arms. O Lakşmaņa, do you exert yourself to break through his* mighty-army; and when the ranks are broken, the son of the Rákşasa-lord shall be visible. * Indrajit's, that is.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.984,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"762ea1708ca29e08b8f10515a3d30e0e291fa98ae9261e96bbbe58d75f646382","compact":"a7de6bcc0a90e07da428f4d96965dc095b027a04346b999ecb2ea3d68b543ee5","nasal":"1e5a00b9e7ed8f6650ca05efcceb9609fd561ea1b41b88b27938c419bb9d322f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":3,"english":"Scattering among the foes shafts resembling Indra's thunder-bolt, charge him while he has not yet finished this ceremony.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0f5b46b4edcf7f015edc31c5e78037dc1d84791a7f4090363c160f0fc111a392","compact":"3038b23e547088520419b78fef5ccf720fdeb1476d5eb092e7eca90405fb9c2f","nasal":"4daa2f8c2ed572acafb95a468eebc9f18e73728c93677448c5c67a70411e80e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":4,"english":"Slay, O hero, this wicked one, this son of Ravana, given to illusion, and of terrific feats, the fear of all the worlds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"244ec9dccdb908d3926e001fc2a1c0742f1113e1dea73eea715c5151e4e71495","compact":"e021cac3a47a5c7932c9176d6dd21c7c7f0a05d035df1f2601e72984191fa63d","nasal":"e021cac3a47a5c7932c9176d6dd21c7c7f0a05d035df1f2601e72984191fa63d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":5,"english":"Hearing Vibhisana's.words, Laksmana graced with auspicious marks began to shower arrows on the son of the Raksasa-chief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d7dc3c1e5b4ce236fc15a983563ac6924eb9156858798823844e2ffd99b853a5","compact":"21b61da02911e82006f6d067ae73514ba34919622c29ffe3650687efe95b5fcd","nasal":"ee8ddd6e556a4d78388ba0832094debe50c272f0d5f92d91802c908d9251ab51"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":6,"english":"And bears and monkeys, given to fighting excellently with trees, in a body rushed towards that army (of Rākşasa) drawn up there.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"000156c692c432c60b9dfb83f8ac1cc8a16a27dc12b36daad2baffe9cc387e65","compact":"63c58751c8e790a8d5cf78431a21bcf220d3a9a368c22cba9b2ecae566f2318a","nasal":"9d65f1df12c1cf2c5e030240109002ebd233571eaadb31f8fa7ba762e52599ca"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":7,"english":"The Rākşasas (on their part) burning to slaughter the monkey-forces, rushed in the encounter with sharpened shafts and darts and tomaras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.629,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5094eeef3e54be2400767b2275a30b7c608e14bad7abe88511d3f9a27f247895","compact":"c4303a8b7804338dab9b38bb4f1eee5afe1ff84e82e7d2fbaeb487322d4b770a","nasal":"b059081baa9dbe57ca5a65e476d61a4e3dcb45bed5fb60a380073dba6f6dc3c5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":8,"english":"There took place a tremendous onslaught of the monkeys and the Raksasas. And Lankā resounded all around with that mighty tumult; and the sky was covered with weapons of various shapes, and whetted arrows and trees and dreadful upraised mountain-tops.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f22b655dcb281da6c6ff32a3988895d0c34bf10ff560363ce865ab460557e761","compact":"1c5ccee525074ea9172b0faab23cf5a15eac8c1a7c66f16dcdfbb19a9fbe5caf","nasal":"15ed3fcd61fc94743bd11e7b2f8f7e38fc63050e10f5782c28d17d355df1a40c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":9,"english":"There took place a tremendous onslaught of the monkeys and the Raksasas. And Lankā resounded all around with that mighty tumult; and the sky was covered with weapons of various shapes, and whetted arrows and trees and dreadful upraised mountain-tops.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.829,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84843826a3ca4e3316b3450437e7e025b4de83f4c76f6ae0de5da8151f789c5c","compact":"ac27df3a72e696a5a6afff8b65f4b25b045dcaa14ab4864405c3389814e34566","nasal":"a8468248c88b64bd67d45a6d212c4fcda6776abb5d73b9150a1d2b7358f67daf"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":10,"english":"Rākşasas having frightful faces and arms, playing their arms among the foremost monkeys, began to spread terror (there).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.883,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b6a3b883a9d1694c73d0cf773cf948a0ee2eac4e860d65ade7849be54f5cb75f","compact":"117f4ec074c05dc977b10d7ba899dfcec2e2ca0994304e5f8d2e6a1599ea04b9","nasal":"6fd564450513db083f0b481e2bd8c7bc269709f4d1a92f6ce9f9c42e03dd239a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":11,"english":"In the same way the monkeys in the conflict fell to slaying and wounding the Rākşasas with trees and hill-tops.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"928946dceae9ae4de5a301607a262e0ed40a8cf85a6a6d7bcf55b45e7c64363c","compact":"462a0735e2a25cd126794dddb38d268975