. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8abc641ac15094f380606857f044ae17cf82346b967478d4fd9de4071bbca246","compact":"8485e88012097e0f07fd14219f235de08296fff37b0c00f0c65d748f6cb17978","nasal":"ced687bbdbed6fb6b04644e40930425878c81b4095d74611e08090bfcc4ee26b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-24","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":24,"english":"Indrajit saw that foremost of monkeys resembling a hill, the offspring of the Windgod possessing himself if calmness, while destroying his foes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.683,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073024","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c6cea04b46dcfbed0c4ca596b14ea7b1582fd1501997d9cceda5d857a0d3830","compact":"0da0524c7912d84509834b2e00970b59431bed38b9508252dfce22c8a6285610","nasal":"f9c9fc5e4d0f236a82801f2bef0389b6808413686fe6988b6420f9e001fac4dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-25","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":25,"english":"Thereat, be* addressed his charioteer, saying, \"Go where the monkeys is. Being disregarded by the Raksasas, he makes havoc among us.\" *Indrajit.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073025","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9ff3e758680ba056fdc4b410b024fd5b0ed8a0ccd950dc10b78c5404a97e6ec6","compact":"a19c9874d98e0d1e4ce93ccb406fb6e94ece51a4c39b71ce0fd9a961cf7b488d","nasal":"a19c9874d98e0d1e4ce93ccb406fb6e94ece51a4c39b71ce0fd9a961cf7b488d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-26","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":26,"english":"Thus accosted by him, the charioteer went where the Wind-god's offspring was, carrying the exceedingly invincible Indrajit seated on the car.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073026","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c6c8e3926ca6e3cc0c50908da2c0e906a8d325598db65d3eae6a96b19d16b490","compact":"b1395b7a4cd0cffed19972700c4265bceef1cfb45cd6f94d8616944bc2765ca5","nasal":"31c0c3894663fef43220c2aa290b888d50bfddb098f0b44eff0b0d6f4c3b8dd6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-27","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":27,"english":"And rushing forward, that irrepressible one the Rākşasas-began to shower on the monkey's head arrows and swords and pațțišas and scimitars and axes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.614,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4aa63ab11e895fb850b2a240d2b33ee8c4c88b71c7bc6d203c5ec134fdc994bd","compact":"9a13ef657416c156fec1b442ac880c3aabe45606f00a7615e26553e48ce6bd98","nasal":"9a13ef657416c156fec1b442ac880c3aabe45606f00a7615e26553e48ce6bd98"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":28,"english":"And bearing all those dreadful arms, the Wind-god's offspring, overcome with a mighty rage said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a208cd1fe070c807103b150e5e284ef97a6007ff82cc3e61d6fe687ee71ab912","compact":"465b79e1fb85176d2cd6982327d55194c7c5a5157eb2978a1b22817da75b8810","nasal":"465b79e1fb85176d2cd6982327d55194c7c5a5157eb2978a1b22817da75b8810"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":29,"english":"O wicked-minded son of Rävaņa, if you are a hero, fight on. Combat with me with your arms.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"563134daa319696e968933f677e66fb4509ef25d1d061325c624747ad0114318","compact":"6a167cd5ee50dc3163686a8182d9f36000acf9840124b6e4ddf7dff2e98a731d","nasal":"6a167cd5ee50dc3163686a8182d9f36000acf9840124b6e4ddf7dff2e98a731d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-30","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":30,"english":"If in the encounter, you bear my impetus, then, O you of perverse sense, you indeed are the foremost of Rākşasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f1054b88697b96557b065be0a276073af9d8169f855ac7e91c184b763ae0f517","compact":"f46adf069938e90a4d8e02d2f3f75d8770511d79c3ac69ebe43cda42eb85daab","nasal":"203eaa9227f35da3dad3f23df91aa9abaafc85b92f2652ccd3eda27c7830ae5a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":31,"english":"Then Vibhīşana pointed out to Lakşmaņa the son of Ravana, who with his bow upraised, was eager to slay Hanumān.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b3ea24b08405e08f60aa055527e517d728ea519d718c40f21b0f0117ce6d78cd","compact":"57694f8cc8c3c92decd98c8e1452647b3235aaed5ad28694c62e6495b8328ff1","nasal":"3b59b868b0eff983bbfa941216a0dfc9891d6758530b4b95e57d1ef3b2df61fb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":32,"english":"This one that, mounted on his car, is eager to slay Hanumăn, is the son of Rāvaņa that has vanquished Vasava himself (in battle). Do you, O son of Sumitrā, with peerless shafts capable of resisting enemies, dreadful, and competent to finish the lives (of foes), slay the son of Ravana.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.907,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073032","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d8a75a4e8108296f64857e8f8d7f9fd037b6643bce24cf9ca94adcd8df2cb284","compact":"cd92ea114caa7a80136fea1fc039c2bcb19df595fdba3e755e3927ef57df57dc","nasal":"f248d6ceb97b8e15b599ccafaadf25402087d45123dc3f0b2c2ab8d6917aba4a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":33,"english":"This one that, mounted on his car, is eager to slay Hanumăn, is the son of Rāvaņa that has vanquished Vasava himself (in battle). Do you, O son of Sumitrā, with peerless shafts capable of resisting enemies, dreadful, and competent to finish the lives (of foes), slay the son of Ravana.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.683,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6c5d722a9bb2c52a9bdd47f17e18eea5766570c7636e31b0e0e70788121464c8","compact":"69df7c89551ce52195352e09b7fae427d7ef67d3d56a7049626f610d40f0f21a","nasal":"1c3464abeaf470910bcd1581e3e48a9330e17e3853122737878caf14aa7d1ef3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-73-34","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":73,"verse":34,"english":"Thus accosted by Vibhīşaņa terrific to foes, that high-souled one saw (Indrajit) of dreadful prowess, difficult to gut at, and resembling a hill, stationed on his car.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-86-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6073034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","engl